1. Which required Data Science course may be waived according to the general FAQ?
According to the general FAQ, of the required Data Science courses, only DS-GA 1002 may be waived [1].

2. What materials must be submitted for review for a waiver?
The following materials generally need to be submitted and reviewed for a waiver of DS-GA 1002:
– Undergraduate or Graduate Transcripts (must be translated);
– The course(s) that you will be using to waive the required course should be highlighted. The grade(s) you received in the course(s) should be highlighted as well;
– Syllabi of the course(s) that you will be using to waive the required course (must be translated);
– If available, course website [1].

All required information is provided in source [1].

**Part: Which required Data Science course may be waived, and what materials must be submitted for review according to the general FAQ?**

According to the general FAQ, of the required Data Science courses, only DS-GA 1002 may be waived. The materials that must be submitted and reviewed for the waiver process generally include:
- Undergraduate or Graduate Transcripts (must be translated);
- The course(s) being used to waive the required course should be highlighted, including the grade(s) received;
- Syllabi of the course(s) used to waive the required course (must be translated);
- If available, the course website [1].

